          "solution": "Shortest Lyman wavelength ($\\infty\\to1$ in H): $\\frac1\\lambda=R$.<br>Longest Balmer wavelength in $\\text{He}^+$ ($Z=2$, $3\\to2$): $\\frac1{\\lambda'}=RZ^2\\left(\\frac14-\\frac19\\right)=4R\\times\\frac5{36}=\\frac{5R}9$, so $\\lambda'=\\frac{9}{5R}=\\frac{9\\lambda}5$.<br><b>Answer: (2)</b>"
